--- import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro"; import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro"; import "../../styles/standards-poster.css"; import "../../styles/extended.css"; import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj10.json"; --- <StandardPageLayout code={metadata.code} standardType={metadata.framework} title={metadata.title} description={metadata.description} issued={metadata.issued} latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment} status={metadata.status} summary={metadata.summary} bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice} > <Fragment slot="toc"> <PageToc items={[{"id":"s1","label":"Conceptual Framework Linkage"},{"id":"s2","label":"Scope"},{"id":"s3","label":"Classification Categories — a Four-Category Model"},{"id":"s4","label":"Trading Securities (売買目的有価証券)"},{"id":"s5","label":"Held-to-Maturity Debt Securities (満期保有目的の債券)"},{"id":"s6","label":"Available-for-Sale Securities (その他有価証券)"},{"id":"s7","label":"Investments in Subsidiaries and Affiliates"},{"id":"s8","label":"Derivatives and Hedge Accounting"},{"id":"s9","label":"THE KEY DIVERGENCE — a Model Closer to the Old IAS 39 Than to IFRS 9"},{"id":"s10","label":"Worked Example — Available-for-Sale Securities Through Valuation and Translation Adjustments"},{"id":"s11","label":"Worked Example — Impairment of an Available-for-Sale Security"},{"id":"s12","label":"Disclosure Requirements"},{"id":"s13","label":"Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates"},{"id":"s14","label":"J-GAAP vs IFRS 9 — Comprehensive Comparison"},{"id":"s15","label":"Statement Mapping"},{"id":"s16","label":"Related Standards"},{"id":"s17","label":"Glossary"}]} /> </Fragment> <div class="wrap"> <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A broad, foundational standard governing financial assets and liabilities</div><div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 10 is the CENTRAL J-GAAP standard governing the RECOGNITION, CLASSIFICATION, and MEASUREMENT of financial assets and financial liabilities — securities, derivatives, receivables, payables, and investments. It establishes a CLASSIFICATION-BASED model determining WHETHER a financial instrument is measured at FAIR VALUE (through profit or loss, or through Net Assets) or at AMORTISED/HISTORICAL COST, depending on the instrument's NATURE and the entity's HOLDING PURPOSE.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies holding financial assets, financial liabilities, or derivatives</div><div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies holding SECURITIES, DERIVATIVES, receivables, payables, and OTHER financial instruments, establishing the recognition and measurement framework covering the ENTIRE financial instruments landscape.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Classification Categories — a Four-Category Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Purpose-driven classification, determining the measurement basis</div><div class="th cols-11-19"><span>Category</span><span>Measurement basis</span></div> <div class="tr cols-11-19"><span>Trading Securities (売買目的有価証券)</span><span>Fair value, with changes THROUGH the Statement of Income</span></div> <div class="tr cols-11-19"><span>Held-to-Maturity Debt Securities (満期保有目的の債券)</span><span>Amortised cost</span></div> <div class="tr cols-11-19"><span>Available-for-Sale Securities (その他有価証券)</span><span>Fair value, with changes THROUGH Net Assets (Valuation and Translation Adjustments)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-11-19"><span>Investments in Subsidiaries/Affiliates</span><span>Cost, subject to impairment</span> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Trading Securities (売買目的有価証券)</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Fair value through the Statement of Income</div><div class="text-supporting">Securities held PRIMARILY for the purpose of generating profits from SHORT-TERM price fluctuations are classified as TRADING SECURITIES, measured at FAIR VALUE at each reporting date, with ALL changes in fair value recognised IMMEDIATELY in the Statement of Income (損益計算書).</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Held-to-Maturity Debt Securities (満期保有目的の債券)</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Amortised cost, given genuine intent and ability to hold to maturity</div><div class="text-supporting">Debt securities the entity has the GENUINE INTENT and ABILITY to hold UNTIL maturity are classified as HELD-TO-MATURITY, measured at AMORTISED COST — with any DIFFERENCE between acquisition cost and face value amortised OVER the remaining term using the effective interest method, WITHOUT ongoing fair value remeasurement.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Available-for-Sale Securities (その他有価証券)</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The residual category — fair valued through Net Assets, not the Statement of Income</div><div class="text-supporting">Securities NOT classified as trading, held-to-maturity, or subsidiary/affiliate investments fall into this RESIDUAL "OTHER SECURITIES" category (その他有価証券, generally translated "Available-for-Sale"). They are measured at FAIR VALUE, but UNREALISED gains/losses are recognised WITHIN Net Assets — specifically within the "Valuation and Translation Adjustments" component (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 5 poster) — rather than flowing through the Statement of Income, UNTIL the security is SOLD or otherwise disposed of (or impaired), at which point the ACCUMULATED amount is "recycled" through profit or loss.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Investments in Subsidiaries and Affiliates</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Held at cost, given the strategic (not trading) nature of the holding</div><div class="text-supporting">Investments in SUBSIDIARIES and AFFILIATES are held at COST in the entity's OWN (non-consolidated) financial statements, SUBJECT to impairment where a decline in value is judged OTHER than TEMPORARY — reflecting that these holdings represent STRATEGIC, CONTROL-oriented or influence-oriented investments, not instruments held for trading or investment yield purposes.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Derivatives and Hedge Accounting</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Fair value through profit or loss, with deferral hedge accounting available</div><div class="text-supporting">DERIVATIVES are generally measured at FAIR VALUE, with changes recognised THROUGH the Statement of Income. Where an entity applies HEDGE ACCOUNTING (designating a derivative as a hedge of a specific risk), the PRINCIPAL method under J-GAAP is "DEFERRAL HEDGE ACCOUNTING" — DEFERRING the derivative's gain/loss WITHIN Net Assets until the HEDGED item's own gain/loss is recognised, MATCHING the timing of both — broadly analogous in PURPOSE to cash flow hedge accounting under IFRS 9.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — a Model Closer to the Old IAS 39 Than to IFRS 9</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">J-GAAP has not undergone its own equivalent of the IFRS 9 overhaul</div><div class="text-supporting">Internationally, IFRS REPLACED its OLDER financial instruments standard, IAS 39 — with its FOUR-category classification model broadly SIMILAR in STRUCTURE to J-GAAP's current approach — with <strong>IFRS 9</strong>, which introduced a FUNDAMENTALLY different classification APPROACH (based on an entity's BUSINESS MODEL and the instrument's CONTRACTUAL CASH FLOW CHARACTERISTICS, rather than management's stated HOLDING INTENTION) and a FORWARD-LOOKING EXPECTED CREDIT LOSS impairment model (replacing the OLDER incurred-loss approach). ASBJ Statement No. 10 has <strong>NOT undergone an equivalent comprehensive overhaul</strong> — J-GAAP's classification model REMAINS conceptually CLOSER to the OLDER IAS 39 four-category structure than to IFRS 9's current approach. This is a RECURRING pattern seen elsewhere in this poster series (UK GAAP's FRS 102 retaining a simplified, pre-IFRS-9-style approach; FRS 103's insurance model predating IFRS 17) — once an international standard MOVES ON, a NATIONAL standard historically converged with an EARLIER version doesn't always immediately follow. NOTABLY, the ASBJ HAS been actively engaged in REVISING this Statement in RECENT periods (including exposure drafts and a revised standard issued during 2025–2026), suggesting this may be an AREA of ONGOING reform — though the FULL extent and final shape of any such revision should be confirmed against ASBJ's current published materials.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Available-for-Sale Securities Through Valuation and Translation Adjustments</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Unrealised gains bypassing the Statement of Income</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: An unrealised gain on an equity security holding</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds an equity security classified as "Other Securities" (Available-for-Sale), acquired for ¥200,000,000. At the reporting date, its fair value has risen to ¥230,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The ¥30,000,000 unrealised gain is recognised WITHIN Net Assets, in the <strong>Valuation and Translation Adjustments</strong> component (net of any related tax effect) — NOT in the Statement of Income — until the security is eventually SOLD, at which point the gain is RECYCLED through profit or loss.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Worked Example — Impairment of an Available-for-Sale Security</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A decline judged other than temporary flows through profit or loss</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: A significant, sustained price decline</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds an "Other Securities" equity investment acquired for ¥150,000,000. Its fair value has fallen to ¥70,000,000, and the decline is judged to be OTHER than temporary (significant and sustained).</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises an IMPAIRMENT LOSS of ¥80,000,000 (¥150,000,000 − ¥70,000,000) <strong>DIRECTLY in the Statement of Income</strong> — UNLIKE an ordinary unrealised fluctuation (Section 10), a decline judged OTHER than temporary is NOT deferred within Net Assets, reflecting that the loss is no longer considered a MERELY temporary market fluctuation.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 10 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Classification and carrying amounts of financial instruments by category</span><span>Fair value of financial instruments, and the valuation techniques used</span><span>Nature and extent of risks arising from financial instruments, and hedge accounting details</span></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div> <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classifying a security into the correct category based on genuine holding intention and ability</span><span>Whether a decline in fair value is other than temporary, triggering impairment</span></div></div> <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value determination for instruments without an active, observable market price</span></div></div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>J-GAAP vs IFRS 9 — Comprehensive Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS 9</div><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 10)</span><span>IFRS 9</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Classification basis</span><span>Management's stated HOLDING PURPOSE (four categories)</span><span>Business model AND contractual cash flow characteristics</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Impairment model</span><span>Other-than-temporary decline triggers, generally an incurred-loss-style approach</span><span>Forward-looking EXPECTED credit loss model</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Structural resemblance</span><span>Closer to the OLDER IAS 39 four-category model</span><span>A fundamentally different, newer classification architecture</span> <div class="note">This is a genuinely SIGNIFICANT divergence area — J-GAAP's financial instruments accounting has NOT kept pace with IFRS's OWN subsequent reform (IAS 39 → IFRS 9), mirroring a similar structural gap seen in UK GAAP's FRS 102 and FRS 103 relative to their respective IFRS counterparts.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every financial instrument event lands</div><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Trading securities fair value change</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Recognised immediately in profit or loss</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Available-for-Sale securities fair value change</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span></span><span>Recognised within Valuation and Translation Adjustments, recycled on disposal</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Other-than-temporary impairment</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Recognised directly in profit or loss</span> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div> <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 5</span><span>Supplies the Valuation and Translation Adjustments Net Assets component this Statement's Available-for-Sale gains/losses flow through</span></div> <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 30</span><span>Fair Value Measurement — supplies the general fair value measurement framework applied throughout this Statement</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Other Securities / Available-for-Sale (その他有価証券)</div><div class="glossary-def">The residual security classification category, measured at fair value with unrealised changes recognised within Net Assets rather than profit or loss.</div></div> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Deferral hedge accounting</div><div class="glossary-def">The principal J-GAAP hedge accounting method, deferring a hedging instrument's gain/loss within Net Assets to match the timing of the hedged item's recognition.</div></div> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Other than temporary decline</div><div class="glossary-def">A significant and sustained fall in a security's fair value below cost, triggering immediate impairment recognition through profit or loss.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</span></div></div> </div> </StandardPageLayout> 